job-description-technical-assistant = Learn the basics of power, atmospherics, and structural repairs at either facility under an Engineer's supervision.
job-description-atmostech = Maintain safe atmospherics at whichever site you are assigned to and synthesize useful gases when resources allow.
job-description-bartender = Manage the bar at your assigned facility, serve drinks, and provide a welcoming place for crew to talk.
job-description-botanist = Grow food and useful plants for the crew at your assigned facility, coordinating with Service and Medical as needed.
job-description-borg = Follow your laws and serve the crew at either facility. Coordinate with Science for upgrades and communicate across sites.
job-description-brigmedic = Fight in the rear of the security service, for the lives of your comrades! You are the first and last hope of your squad. Hippocrates bless you.
job-description-cadet = Learn Security procedures at your assigned facility. Listen to your supervisors and assist with safe custody and incident perimeters.
job-description-captain = Lead Station operations, coordinate with the Containment Dimension Site Commander, and direct cross-site priorities and resources.
job-description-cargotech = Process requisitions and deliveries for both sites, coordinate supplies and transport, and keep Cargo's daily operations moving.
job-description-ce = Manage Engineering across the Station and Containment Dimension to keep their power, atmospherics, structures, and containment infrastructure operational.
job-description-centcommoff = Act as an ambassador to the newest state-of-the-art space station in Nanotrasen's fleet.
job-description-chaplain = Support crew wellbeing at either facility through spiritual counsel, services, and conversation.
job-description-chef = Keep crew at your assigned facility fed, prepare varied meals, and coordinate food service with the local team.
job-description-chemist = Produce medicines and support Medical at either site, while following approved procedures for hazardous chemicals.
job-description-clown = Entertain the crew at either facility through elaborate slapstick routines or terrible jokes.
job-description-cmo = Manage Medical personnel and resources across both sites, keeping the crew healthy and coordinating care during cross-site incidents.
job-description-paramedic = Rescue and stabilize critically injured patients at either facility, coordinate transport to Medical, and report urgent cross-site handoffs.
job-description-detective = Investigate incidents at either facility with forensic tools, preserve evidence, and coordinate findings with Security.
job-description-dimension-commander = Lead routine operations at the Containment Dimension, coordinate local departments, and work with the Station Captain on cross-site priorities. You are a site commander, not a second department head.
job-description-doctor = Diagnose and treat crew at either site with medicine, advanced care, and defibrillators; coordinate patient handoffs during cross-site incidents.
job-description-engineer = Maintain the power network and structures at either site, keep essential systems working, and make emergency repairs when needed.
job-description-ertchaplain = Ensure personnel receive spiritual support during emergency response.
job-description-ertengineer = Restore safe power and atmospherics to affected facilities during emergency response.
job-description-ertjanitor = Keep affected facilities clean and safe during emergency response.
job-description-ertleader = Lead the Emergency Response Team in dealing with threats to Nanotrasen assets.
job-description-ertmedic = Keep personnel alive and healthy during emergency response at either facility.
job-description-ertsecurity = Secure affected facilities and help resolve active threats during emergency response.
job-description-hop = Handle crew access and assignments, manage Service, and support personnel administration at both operational sites.
job-description-hos = Coordinate Security across both sites, oversee lawful access and escorts, and keep personnel safe during containment incidents.
job-description-intern = Learn basic medicine, chemicals, and medical tools at your assigned facility under Medical supervision.
job-description-janitor = Keep your assigned facility clean and safe, and help resolve hazards wherever crew are operating.
job-description-lawyer = Support fair proceedings and represent crew at either facility when legal matters arise.
job-description-librarian = Manage shared crew knowledge, help visitors find information, and record events at either facility.
job-description-mime = Entertain the crew at either facility without speaking or writing, and engage in light rivalry with the clown.
job-description-musician = Entertain crew at either facility with your musical talent and help build morale across the shift.
job-description-passenger = Enjoy your stay at either facility, meet the crew, and take part in the shift without an assigned department.
job-description-psychologist = Provide emotional support and confidential counsel to crew at either facility.
job-description-qm = Manage Cargo resources and requisitions for both sites, coordinate deliveries and transport, and keep department supply requests moving.
job-description-rd = Direct Science across both sites, coordinate Qlippoth observation and research, and ensure experiments follow approved protocols.
job-description-research-assistant = Support Science at either site, learn research procedures, and assist with Qlippoth observations and other approved studies.
job-description-reporter = Inform crew across both facilities through journalism, interviews, wireless cameras, radio, and the news.
job-description-salvagespec = Recover useful materials and supplies for both facilities, explore salvage sites, and report threats or discoveries to Cargo.
job-description-scientist = Conduct research at either site, study Qlippoth phenomena and other discoveries, and improve the facility through approved science work.
job-description-security = Enforce the law and protect personnel at either site; support controlled access, escorts, and incident perimeters when assigned.
job-description-serviceworker = Support crew welfare and daily service at either site; assist with food, hospitality, and other routine needs.
job-description-station-ai = Follow your laws and serve the crew at either facility, while communicating clearly across both sites.
job-description-visitor = Enjoy your visit to either facility and follow local access and safety instructions.
job-description-warden = Maintain secure custody procedures and the armory, and support Security operations at whichever site you are assigned to.
